.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M006.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"071072c9","parentId":"522fa694","timestamp":"2026-05-12T01:52:50.599Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a very clear picture. Let me compile the gray areas:\n\n**Current structure problem:**\n- The Python package `heretek_swarm/` lives nested inside `heretek-swarm/` (the project subdir)\n- The name `heretek-swarm` for the project subdir is confusing — it looks like `heretek_swarm` but with a dash\n- The plan from the ROADMAP says: `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/`\n\n**Gray areas I see:**\n\n1. **`src/` at repo root** — Contains `cli.py` (19KB, full CLI application) and its own `__init__.py`. It looks like a separate entry-point package. Should this stay at root, move into `backend/`, or be absorbed into `heretek_swarm/cli/`? The inner `heretek_swarm/` already has a `cli.py` (63KB!) and a `cli/` subpackage. So there are TWO CLI entry points. This is a major gray area.\n\n2. **Root-level `tests/` vs `heretek-swarm/tests/`** — Root has ~50 test files (the main suite). Inner has ~16 test files. The inner tests look like consensus/goal tests specifically. Do both move into `backend/tests/`?\n\n3. **Duplicate directories**: `agent_workspace/` exists at both root and inner, with slightly different agent sets (root has `alpha-brain` and `gamma` that inner doesn't). `.actor_states/` and `.benchmarks/` exist at both levels. These need to be consolidated.\n\n4. **Root `docs/`** is extensive (~20 files) vs inner `docs/` which only has `actors/`. Do root docs move into `backend/docs/` or stay root?\n\n5. **Root `migrations/`** — Only exists at root. Goes into `backend/`?\n\n6. **Root `audit/`** directory — What is this?\n\n7. **The `.claude/` directory** only exists inside `heretek-swarm/`. Move into `backend/`?\n\n8. **The `heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm.egg-info/`** — build artifact, probably stays/gitignored.\n\nNow, the project shape says it's complex. So I need to use structured questions.\n\nLet me ask the first round of structured questions focusing on the most consequential unknowns.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Good — I have a clear picture of the repo now. Let me summarize the key gray areas before asking questions.\n\n**Current structure problem:**\n- `heretek-swarm/` (project subdir) contains `heretek_swarm/` (Python package) — the dash-vs-underscore naming is confusing\n- The plan (`heretek-swarm/` → `backend/`) is the right fix, but there are several things that exist both at root and inside `heretek-swarm/`:\n\n| Thing | Root | Inner (`heretek-swarm/`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/` | ~50 files (main suite) | ~16 files (consensus/goal) |\n| `agent_workspace/` | 9 agents | 6 agents (missing alpha-brain, gamma) |\n| `docs/` | ~20 files | Only `actors/` |\n| `.actor_states/` | yes | yes |\n| `.benchmarks/` | yes | yes |\n\nPlus: `src/` at root is a separate package (with `cli.py`, 19KB) that may shadow or duplicate `heretek_swarm/cli.py` (63KB) inside.\n\n---"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_l5nd5gxt","name":"ask_user_questions","arguments":{"questions":[{"header":"src/ & CLI","id":"src_cli_fate","options":[{"description":"Move src/ into backend/ alongside heretek_swarm/, consolidate the two CLI surfaces into one","label":"Merge into backend/ (Recommended)","preview":"backend/\n├── heretek_swarm/   # existing Python package\n├── src/             # CLI entry point (merged)\n├── tests/           # consolidated tests\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── Dockerfile"},{"description":"heretek_swarm/cli.py is the canonical CLI; root src/ is redundant/legacy","label":"Delete src/ entirely","preview":"Remove root src/cli.py (19KB) and src/__init__.py.\nAll CLI entry points are through heretek_swarm/cli.py (63KB).\nCI entry points must change to reference the new path."},{"description":"src/ stays where it is as a thin entry point, only heretek-swarm/ becomes backend/","label":"Leave src/ at root"}],"question":"The root-level src/ directory contains cli.py (19KB) plus its own __init__.py, but heretek_swarm/ already has cli.py (63KB) and a cli/ subpackage. What should happen to root src/?"},{"header":"Root tests/","id":"root_tests_fate","options":[{"description":"Move root tests/ and inner tests/ into one backend/tests/ directory; CI points to backend/tests/","label":"Consolidate into backend/tests/ (Recommended)","preview":"backend/\n├── heretek_swarm/\n├── tests/          # all 66+ test files consolidated\n│   ├── unit/\n│   ├── integration/\n│   └── conftest.py\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── Dockerfile"},{"description":"Root tests stay root-level as main suite; only inner heretek-swarm/tests/ moves into backend/","label":"Keep separate: root=tests/, backend=tests/"},{"description":"Root tests/ was an older suite; only inner heretek-swarm/tests/ moves into backend/tests/","label":"Only backend/tests/ survives, root tests deleted"}],"question":"The root tests/ (~50 files) is the main test suite. heretek-swarm/tests/ (~16 files) looks like inner integration tests. Where should tests go in the restructured repo?"},{"header":"Docs & Workspace","id":"docs_workspace_fate","options":[{"description":"Root docs/ and agent_workspace/ are canonical; delete the inner partial copies; both stay at repo root","label":"Consolidate root, delete inner (Recommended)","preview":"repo-root/\n├── backend/         # renamed from heretek-swarm/\n├── docs/            # canonical, at root\n├── agent_workspace/ # canonical, at root (9 agents)\n├── swarm-dashboard/\n├── .github/\n└── docker-compose.yml"},{"description":"All docs and workspace move into backend/docs/ and backend/agent_workspace/","label":"Move everything into backend/"},{"description":"Root is canonical; inner has symlinks or thin references pointing to root","label":"Consolidate root, sync inner as pointer"}],"question":"docs/ and agent_workspace/ exist at both root and inside heretek-swarm/. The inner copies are partial. How should these be handled?"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":164642,"output":1634,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":166276,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778550733229}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"7419228c","parentId":"cca57859","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:09:52.161Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zaodmgk1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Heretek Swarm — Project Status\n\n## Active Milestone\n\n**None** — M007 awaits planning.\n\n## Completed Milestones\n\n| ID | Title | Completed | Outcome |\n|----|-------|-----------|---------|\n| M001 | Collapse dual actors/ directory into one canonical location | 2025-05-07 | ✅ Canonical `heretek_swarm/actors/__init__.py` established; shim files deleted |\n| M002 | Unify validation into a single entry point | 2026-05-07 | ✅ ValidationMixin is single source of truth; backward-compat shims in place |\n| M003 | Type-seal Mixin contracts and make stub injection first-class | 2026-05-10 | ✅ 6 mixin classes with fail-fast __init__ guards; 6 protocol stub classes as first-class kwargs; 14 tests |\n| M004 | Add integration test scaffold and CI surface | 2026-05-10 | ✅ 658-test baseline verified, 26 lifecycle smoke tests for all 24 AgentActor subclasses, pass/fail-gated CI with Ruff quality gate |\n| M005 | Document architecture and compress flat actor API surface | 2026-05-12 | ✅ ARCHITECTURE.md (12 sections, all 10 mixins), actors/README.md (6 sections, 23-agent table), structlog consolidated to single entry point, 14 flat files converted to thin re-exports, uniform subpackage convention for all 24 agents |\n| M006 | Audit and plan repository restructure | 2026-05-12 | ✅ 4-document migration blueprint (FILE_INVENTORY.md, IMPORT_MAP.md, CI_IMPACT.md, M006-PLAN.md) covering 856 files, 429 Python imports, 22 config change sites; M007-ready with 9-task decomposition |\n\n## Current State\n\n- **Repository structure**: `heretek-swarm/` project subdirectory contains the Python package `heretek_swarm/`. M006 produced a complete migration plan to rename `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/` via a single `git mv` + 22 config line edits with zero Python code changes. Execution deferred to M007.\n- **Test infrastructure**: pytest 9.0.3 collects ~370 unit tests (all passing). 26 parameterized lifecycle smoke tests cover all 24 AgentActor subclasses plus BehaviorProfiler and ActorSupervisor, using 6 infrastructure-free stubs (StubAccessAnalyzer, StubPatternExtractor, StubTribunal, StubDeliberationEngine, StubLLMProvider, StubEventMesh). Integration tests run separately.\n- **CI pipeline**: GitHub Actions runs unit-only pytest (`-m \"not integration\"`) and ruff check on push/PR to main/develop. Proper pass/fail gating (no `|| true`). Ruff warning gate fails CI at 50+ findings.\n- **Validation architecture**: Unified. `ValidationMixin` in `actors/mixins/validation.py` is the single source of truth for `IMMUTABLE_RULES` (8 security patterns) and `BASELINE_CONFIG` (9 configuration keys). `actors/validation.py` provides backward-compat shims with deprecation notes.\n- **Pydantic models**: All actor message models live in `heretek_swarm/schemas/actors.py` as the canonical import path.\n- **Actors import surface**: Unified. All 24 agent classes import from `heretek_swarm.actors` via `__init__.py` re-export surface. Every agent follows a uniform subpackage convention: complex agents use split pattern (`types.py + agent.py`), simple agents use `agent.py` only. All 14 surviving flat `.py` files are thin re-export stubs with zero class definitions.\n- **Logging**: `logging/config.py` is the single source of truth for structlog configuration. `core.py` imports `get_logger` from the canonical path. `init_logging()` in `otel/logging.py` delegates to `setup_logging()`. Exactly one `structlog.configure()` call exists in the codebase.\n- **Documentation**: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (914 lines, 12 sections) covers the full system: package structure, actor architecture, all 10 mixins, memory system, event mesh, configuration, security, and observability. `docs/actors/README.md` (16.5KB, 6 sections) provides a practical agent creation guide with 23-agent reference table.\n- **Coverage and linting configuration**: Coverage source points to `heretek-swarm/` package root (was broken `src/`). Ruff src roots corrected to `[\"heretek-swarm\", \"tests\"]`. Coverage paths prefix uses `heretek-swarm/`.\n- **Mixin type guards**: All 6 mixin classes have `_validate_dependencies()` guards that raise `TypeError` when a required dependency attribute is `None`.\n- **Stub injection**: 6 protocol stub classes are first-class `AgentActor.__init__` kwargs. Mixin deps use public instance attrs; core deps use private attrs with `value or fallback()` for backward compat. 14 tests in `tests/test_stub_injection.py`.\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- `heretek_swarm/actors/__init__.py` is the single canonical import surface for all agent classes.\n- `ValidationMixin` is the single source of truth for immutable security rules and behavioral baseline configuration.\n- All Pydantic models live in `heretek_swarm/schemas/actors.py`.\n- `actors/base/core.py` delegates validation to `actors/validation.py` only.\n- Mixin deps use public instance attrs (`self.access_analyzer`) for MRO-visible mixin access; core deps use private names (`self._llm_provider`) for internal consumption. Kwargs typed as `Any | None = None` to avoid circular imports.\n- CI uses unit-only test selection with marker-based isolation (`@pytest.mark.integration`); full-service tests run separately.\n- `logging/config.py` is the single source of truth for structlog configuration; all other modules delegate via `setup_logging()`.\n- All 24 agents follow uniform subpackage convention: split pattern (types.py + agent.py) for complex actors, simple pattern (agent.py only) for straightforward ones.\n- Python resolves modules by package name (`heretek_swarm`), not filesystem directory name (`heretek-swarm`). Directory renames are transparent to Python imports as long as pyproject.toml `where`/`source` directives are updated.\n- `swarm-dashboard/` has zero filesystem-level dependencies on the backend directory — fully decoupled.\n"}],"details":{"target":{"kind":"file","action":"read","inputPath":".gsd/PROJECT.md","resolvedPath":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm\\.gsd\\PROJECT.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584192160}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"e895fd70","parentId":"903518db","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:10:07.019Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_50tmrl7p","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"agent_workspace/\naudit/\ndocs/\nheretek-swarm/\nmigrations/\nnode_modules/\nsrc/\nswarm-dashboard/\ntest-results/\ntests/\n"}],"details":{"cwd":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584207019}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"a1c89124","parentId":"52ee863f","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:11:44.755Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02xuamxy","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# M007: Execute repository restructure\n\n**Vision:** Rename the inner Python package directory from heretek-swarm/ to backend/, update all imports, fix CI paths, and verify everything works cleanly. The swarm-dashboard/ frontend is already correctly separated.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- heretek-swarm/ renamed to backend/ via git mv\n- All Python imports updated\n- All CI workflows updated\n- Full test suite passes\n- Git history preserved\n\n## Slices\n\n- [ ] **S01: Rename heretek-swarm/ to backend/ via git mv** `risk:medium` `depends:[]`\n  > After this: Repo at new path with no code changes; only directory moves via git mv.\n\n- [ ] **S02: Rewrite imports and CI paths** `risk:medium` `depends:[S01]`\n  > After this: All Python imports use the new backend/ path; CI passes.\n\n- [ ] **S03: Verify clean clone and full integration** `risk:low` `depends:[S02]`\n  > After this: Fresh clone of the repo works perfectly at new paths.\n\n## Boundary Map\n\n```\nheretek-swarm/                        ← repo root (unchanged)\n├── backend/                          ← heretek-swarm/ renamed\n│   └── heretek_swarm/              ← Python package (unchanged)\n├── swarm-dashboard/                  ← already clean\n├── docs/                             ← already clean\n├── agent_workspace/                  ← already clean\n└── .github/workflows/               ← needs path updates for backend/\n```\n"}],"details":{"target":{"kind":"file","action":"read","inputPath":".gsd/milestones/M007/M007-ROADMAP.md","resolvedPath":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm\\.gsd\\milestones\\M007\\M007-ROADMAP.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584304755}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"0b76a724","parentId":"a1c89124","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:11:44.763Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5ks72x5u","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# M007: Execute repository restructure\n\n**Rename heretek-swarm/ to backend/, rewrite imports, fix CI, verify clean**\n\n## What Happened\n\nM007 executes the restructure planned in M006.\n\n## Cross-Slice Verification\n\n- S01: `test -d backend/heretek_swarm && echo \"OK\"`\n- S02: `pytest backend/tests/ -x -q && grep -r \"heretek-swarm\" .github/workflows/ | wc -l` (should be 0)\n- S03: `npm run build --prefix swarm-dashboard && docker compose build`\n\n## Requirement Changes\n\nNo requirements were modified — this is purely an infrastructure/planning milestone.\n\n## Forward Intelligence\n\n### What the next milestone should know\n- After M007, `backend/heretek_swarm/` is the canonical import path\n- swarm-dashboard/ connects via HTTP (subprocess or API), not Python imports — verify this first\n\n### What's fragile\n- CI workflows still reference `heretek-swarm/` — must update after `git mv`\n- Python's `__init__.py` `__package__` paths may need adjustment after rename\n\n### What assumptions changed\n- The entire rename is just `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/` — nothing else moves\n\n## Files Created/Modified\n\n- `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/` (renamed via git mv)\n- `.github/workflows/*.yml` (path updates)\n- `docker-compose.yml`, `Dockerfile` (path updates)\n- `backend/heretek_swarm/**/*.py` (import rewrites)\n\n---\nid: M007\nprovides:\n  - Clean monorepo structure\n  - Updated CI paths\n  - Verified imports and tests\nkey_decisions:\n  - Using `git mv` to preserve history\n  - Python imports inside backend/ stay as heretek_swarm. (package-relative)\n  - CI workflows use backend/ prefix\npatterns_established: []\nobservability_surfaces: []\nrequirement_outcomes: []\nduration: ~2.5h\nverification_result: pending\ncompleted_at: pending\n"}],"details":{"target":{"kind":"file","action":"read","inputPath":".gsd/milestones/M007/M007-SUMMARY.md","resolvedPath":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm\\.gsd\\milestones\\M007\\M007-SUMMARY.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584304762}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"6e040204","parentId":"3cb36385","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:12:15.230Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a very clear picture. M007 is about executing a repository restructure — renaming `heretek-swarm/` to `backend/` — with a well-documented plan from M006. Let me also read the M006 context and check the current project complexity.\n\nKey things I know:\n1. M006 produced a complete migration plan (FILE_INVENTORY.md, IMPORT_MAP.md, CI_IMPACT.md, M006-PLAN.md)\n2. The plan is very detailed: one `git mv` + 22 line edits across 8 config files, zero Python code changes\n3. M007 already has a ROADMAP.md with 3 slices (S01-S03) and a SUMMARY.md\n4. The project is in interview lane and I need to gather context for M007\n\nLet me check the project complexity and read M006's context for full understanding.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_igf6a1vs","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".gsd/milestones/M006/M006-CONTEXT.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_o0vz194w","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".gsd/milestones/M006/M006-ROADMAP.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":158421,"output":285,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":158706,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778584304764}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"3d89bbaf","parentId":"6e040204","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:12:15.236Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_igf6a1vs","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# M006: Audit and plan repository restructure\n\n**Gathered:** 2026-05-10\n**Status:** Ready for planning\n\n## Project Description\n\nRename the confusing `heretek-swarm/` project subdirectory to `backend/`, consolidate scattered artifacts (tests, workspace, CLI entry points) that are duplicated across root and inner levels, and produce an actionable migration plan for M007 execution.\n\nThe current structure `heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/` uses dash-vs-underscore naming that looks like a typo. The target `backend/heretek_swarm/` makes the role explicit: this is the Python backend, living alongside `swarm-dashboard/` (frontend), `docs/`, and root-level infrastructure.\n\n## Why This Milestone\n\nThe nested `heretek-swarm/` directory is semantically confusing — it contains the Python package `heretek_swarm/` but the dash-vs-underscore naming reads as a mistake. Additionally, artifacts are duplicated across root and inner levels: `tests/` (root ~50 files, inner ~16), `agent_workspace/` (root 9 agents, inner 6 with missing agents), `docs/` (root ~20 files, inner only `actors/`), `.actor_states/`, and `.benchmarks/`. The root `src/` directory contains a separate `cli.py` entry point that may shadow or duplicate `heretek_swarm/cli.py`.\n\nThis milestone audits everything, produces a complete file manifest, import dependency map, CI impact analysis, and an actionable plan — but does NOT execute any moves. Execution is deferred to M007.\n\n## Why Now\n\nM005 completed architectural documentation and compressed the actor API surface. The repository is stable and well-understood. This is the right time to clean up the repo shape before building further features on top of a confusing directory structure.\n\n## User-Visible Outcome\n\n### When this milestone is complete, the user can:\n\n- Read a complete file inventory (FILE_INVENTORY.md) showing every file in the repo, its type, size, purpose, and current→target path\n- Read an import dependency map (IMPORT_MAP.md) showing which packages depend on which, with all `from heretek_swarm.` imports cataloged\n- Read a CI/workflow impact list (CI_IMPACT.md) showing every path reference in workflows, docker-compose, and build configs that will break\n- Read the final migration plan (M006-PLAN.md) that M007 can execute directly — exact file moves, import rewrites, CI path updates, and ordering constraints\n\n### Entry point / environment\n\n- Entry point: Read-only audit — `docs/`, `.gsd/milestones/M006/` artifacts\n- Environment: Local dev\n- Live dependencies involved: none\n\n## Completion Class\n\n- Contract complete means: FILE_INVENTORY.md, IMPORT_MAP.md, CI_IMPACT.md, and M006-PLAN.md exist with complete, validated content\n- Integration complete means: The plan is verified against the actual repo tree and all CI workflow files\n- Operational complete means: M007 can decompose M006-PLAN.md directly into execution tasks without re-auditing\n\n## Final Integrated Acceptance\n\nTo call this milestone complete, we must prove:\n\n- FILE_INVENTORY.md catalogs every source, config, doc, test, CI, and deployment file (excluding .git/, .gsd/, node_modules/, .venv/, __pycache__/)\n- IMPORT_MAP.md shows all Python import dependencies between packages with special attention to `src/` → `heretek_swarm/` cross-references and `swarm-dashboard/` references to the Python package\n- CI_IMPACT.md catalogs all 6 workflow files plus docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile, and pyproject.toml path references that would break under the target structure\n- M006-PLAN.md is the single source of truth for M007 — every file move, import rewrite, and CI fix is specified with ordering constraints\n\n## Architectural Decisions\n\n### Target structure: `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/`\n\n**Decision:** Rename the project subdirectory `heretek-swarm/` to `backend/` using `git mv` to preserve history.\n\n**Rationale:** The name `backend/` makes the directory's role explicit. `heretek-swarm` (with dash) looks like a typo for `heretek_swarm` (with underscore). The target `backend/heretek_swarm/` is clear: backend Python project containing the `heretek_swarm` package.\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Keep `heretek-swarm/` — rejected because the dash-vs-underscore confusion is real and causes cognitive overhead\n- Rename to `python/` or `server/` — rejected; `backend/` is the conventional pairing with `swarm-dashboard/` (frontend)\n\n### Consolidate root `src/` into `backend/`\n\n**Decision:** Move the root-level `src/` directory (containing `cli.py`, `__init__.py`) into `backend/` alongside `heretek_swarm/`, and consolidate the two CLI surfaces.\n\n**Rationale:** Root `src/cli.py` (19KB) and `heretek_swarm/cli.py` (63KB) appear to be two entry points for the same system. Having a CLI package at root when the backend lives in a subdirectory fragments the codebase. After consolidation, `backend/` is the single home for all Python code.\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Delete `src/` entirely — rejected pending investigation of whether `src/` has unique entry points not in `heretek_swarm/cli.py`\n- Leave `src/` at root — rejected; fragments the Python surface across two directory levels\n\n### Consolidate all tests into `backend/tests/`\n\n**Decision:** Move root `tests/` (~50 files) and inner `heretek-swarm/tests/` (~16 files) into a single `backend/tests/` directory.\n\n**Rationale:** Having two test directories at different levels with no clear separation of concerns creates confusion about where tests belong. CI already references `heretek-swarm/` path prefixes.\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Keep separate — rejected; no clear separation rationale exists (both directories contain integration-style tests)\n- Only keep inner tests — rejected; the root test suite is far larger and likely the canonical one\n\n### Root `docs/` and `agent_workspace/` stay at root; inner copies deleted\n\n**Decision:** Root-level `docs/` (~20 files) and `agent_workspace/` (9 agents) are the canonical locations. Delete the partial inner copies (`heretek-swarm/docs/` with only `actors/`, `heretek-swarm/agent_workspace/` with only 6 agents).\n\n**Rationale:** The root copies are larger and more complete. `docs/` at repo root is conventional for discoverability. `agent_workspace/` at root is shared with `swarm-dashboard/`. The inner copies appear to be stale partial mirrors.\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Move everything into `backend/` — rejected; `docs/` at repo root is standard convention, and `agent_workspace/` is shared infrastructure\n- Keep both with symlinks — rejected; adds complexity without benefit\n\n## Error Handling Strategy\n\nM006 is read-only audit work. No error handling is needed for the audit scripts themselves. If a file cannot be read (permissions, encoding), the inventory script should record it as `unreadable` rather than crashing. The produced plan (M006-PLAN.md) should include rollback instructions for M007 execution.\n\n## Risks and Unknowns\n\n- **Two CLI entry points** — `src/cli.py` and `heretek_swarm/cli.py` may have overlapping or divergent functionality. The audit must determine whether both are needed or one supersedes the other.\n- **Import path breakage** — `from heretek_swarm.` imports inside `backend/` may work if PYTHONPATH is set correctly, but any absolute path references in scripts or CI will break.\n- **`swarm-dashboard/` dependencies** — The frontend may import or shell out to the Python package. The audit must check for `subprocess`, `import`, or file-path references crossing the dashboard→backend boundary.\n- **`.actor_states/` and `.benchmarks/` duplication** — Both exist at root and inner levels. It's unclear which is canonical. These are runtime state directories and may need to merge or one deleted.\n- **Inner `pyproject.toml` and `Dockerfile`** — These define the backend package and build. They must move with the rename and have their internal paths updated.\n\n## Existing Codebase / Prior Art\n\n- `heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/` — canonical Python package (~40 subpackages), moves to `backend/heretek_swarm/`\n- `src/cli.py` — separate CLI entry point (19KB), moves into `backend/`\n- `heretek-swarm/pyproject.toml` — backend package definition, moves with rename\n- `heretek-swarm/Dockerfile` — backend container, moves with rename\n- `swarm-dashboard/` — frontend, already correctly placed, stays at root\n- `.github/workflows/` — 6 workflow files with `heretek-swarm/` path references\n- `docker-compose.yml` — references `heretek-swarm/` paths\n- `docs/` — canonical documentation at root\n- `agent_workspace/` — canonical shared workspace at root (9 agents)\n\n## Relevant Requirements\n\n- This milestone is pure infrastructure — it does not directly advance any functional requirements\n- It is a prerequisite for any future milestone that adds new packages or restructures Python module layout\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n\n- Complete file inventory of the repository (excluding build artifacts and tool caches)\n- Python import dependency graph across all packages\n- CI, Docker, and build configuration path audit\n- Actionable migration plan (M006-PLAN.md) for M007 execution\n- Identifying the relationship between the two CLI entry points (`src/cli.py` vs `heretek_swarm/cli.py`)\n\n### Out of Scope / Non-Goals\n\n- Executing any file moves, renames, or import rewrites — deferred to M007\n- Changing Python package internals — only directory structure and import paths\n- Modifying `swarm-dashboard/` code — only auditing whether it references the backend\n- Adding or modifying tests\n\n## Technical Constraints\n\n- All moves must use `git mv` to preserve git history\n- Python imports inside `backend/` using `from heretek_swarm.` should continue to work if PYTHONPATH is set correctly\n- CI workflows outside `backend/` must reference files with `backend/` prefix after the rename\n- Docker compose and Dockerfile paths reference from repo root, not from inside the package\n\n## Integration Points\n\n- `.github/workflows/*.yml` — 6 workflow files with hardcoded `heretek-swarm/` paths that must be updated in M007\n- `docker-compose.yml` — references `heretek-swarm/` build context\n- `swarm-dashboard/` — may reference the Python package via import, subprocess, or file path\n- `pyproject.toml` — package metadata and tool configs that may reference `heretek-swarm/` paths\n\n## Testing Requirements\n\nM006 produces documents, not code changes. Verification is:\n\n- FILE_INVENTORY.md: counts match actual file tree; every line has type, size, path, purpose\n- IMPORT_MAP.md: at least one entry for every `.py` file; cross-package dependencies are flagged\n- CI_IMPACT.md: every workflow file is represented; every `heretek-swarm/` path reference is cataloged\n- M006-PLAN.md: every file move, import rewrite, and CI fix is specified with ordering; `backend/` appears throughout\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- FILE_INVENTORY.md is complete and verifiable against `find` output\n- IMPORT_MAP.md covers all Python files with import statements\n- CI_IMPACT.md covers all 6 workflow files, docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile, pyproject.toml\n- M006-PLAN.md is self-contained — a fresh agent can execute it without re-auditing\n- The two CLI surfaces (`src/cli.py` vs `heretek_swarm/cli.py`) are analyzed and a consolidation decision is documented in the plan\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- **Are `src/cli.py` and `heretek_swarm/cli.py` redundant, or do they serve different entry points?** — The audit must diff their functionality and recommend consolidation or deduplication\n- **Which `.actor_states/` and `.benchmarks/` directories are canonical?** — The inner copies may be legacy; the audit should check modification times and content\n- **Does `swarm-dashboard/` import or shell out to the Python package?** — Must be checked before the rename, as path changes could break the frontend\n- **Should root `migrations/` and `audit/` directories move into `backend/`?** — Pending investigation of their contents and purpose\n"}],"details":{"target":{"kind":"file","action":"read","inputPath":".gsd/milestones/M006/M006-CONTEXT.md","resolvedPath":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm\\.gsd\\milestones\\M006\\M006-CONTEXT.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584335235}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"a8ea6690","parentId":"3d89bbaf","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:12:15.242Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_o0vz194w","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# M006: Audit and plan repository restructure\n\n**Vision:** Map every file in the repo, document what belongs where in the new structure, and produce an actionable migration plan so M007 can execute cleanly.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Full file inventory (PLAN.md)\n- Import dependency map (PLAN.md)\n- CI/workflow impact list (PLAN.md)\n\n## Slices\n\n- [x] **S01: S01** `risk:low` `depends:[]`\n  > After this: After this: a written plan with exact file moves, import rewrites, and CI fixes ready to execute.\n\n## Boundary Map\n\n```\\ncurrent: heretek-swarm/heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/{actors,schemas,validation,...}\\ntarget: backend/heretek_swarm/{actors,schemas,validation,...}\\n```\n"}],"details":{"target":{"kind":"file","action":"read","inputPath":".gsd/milestones/M006/M006-ROADMAP.md","resolvedPath":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm\\.gsd\\milestones\\M006\\M006-ROADMAP.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584335241}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"03ef63e4","parentId":"a8ea6690","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:12:39.002Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the situation. Let me also quickly check the current state of the repo to see if there are any differences from what M006 documented (it was completed on 2026-05-12, and today is 2026-05-10 — wait, that can't be right, M006 completed on 2026-05-12 and the current date in the snapshot is 2026-05-10. Actually the timeline seems odd — M004 completed 2026-05-10, M005 completed 2026-05-12, M006 completed 2026-05-12. The snapshot is from 2026-05-10. This might just be a quirk of how the data was recorded. Let me not worry about the timeline and focus on M007.)\n\nLet me check a few critical things:\n1. What does the current filesystem actually look like?\n2. Are there differences from what M006 expected?\n3. What are the real gray areas for M007?\n\nKey observations from M006-PLAN.md:\n- The plan scoped to rename `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/` + 22 config line edits\n- M006-CONTEXT.md mentions additional scope items that were later refined or descoped in M006-PLAN.md: consolidating `src/` into `backend/`, merging two test directories, deleting inner docs/agent_workspace copies — but these don't appear in the final M006-PLAN.md or M007-ROADMAP.md\n\nWait, let me re-read more carefully. The M006-CONTEXT.md was written as the initial context, and then M006-PLAN.md was the refined output. The M007-ROADMAP.md seems to scope M007 to just the rename + config updates. But there are open questions from M006 that weren't fully resolved... let me check what the current repo actually looks like.\n\nLet me scout the current state to see what's changed since M006.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me scout the current repo state to identify what's real vs. what the plan assumes."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_yahw8ue7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== Top-level dirs ===\" && ls -d */ && echo \"=== heretek-swarm contents ===\" && ls heretek-swarm/ && echo \"=== src/ contents ===\" && ls -la src/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== tests count ===\" && ls tests/*.py 2>/dev/null | wc -l && echo \"=== inner tests? ===\" && ls heretek-swarm/tests/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== agent_workspace root ===\" && ls agent_workspace/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== agent_workspace inner ===\" && ls heretek-swarm/agent_workspace/ 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":161773,"output":628,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":162401,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778584335242}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"0d90e0e8","parentId":"03ef63e4","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:12:39.132Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_yahw8ue7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== Top-level dirs ===\nagent_workspace/\naudit/\ndocs/\nheretek-swarm/\nmigrations/\nnode_modules/\nsrc/\nswarm-dashboard/\ntest-results/\ntests/\n=== heretek-swarm contents ===\nDockerfile\nLICENSE\nagent_workspace\ndocs\nheretek_swarm\nheretek_swarm.db\nheretek_swarm.egg-info\ntest_ws_integration.db\ntests\n=== src/ contents ===\ntotal 45\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 Derek 197608     0 Apr 29 10:03 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 Derek 197608     0 May 12 07:08 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Derek 197608   131 Apr 29 10:03 __init__.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 Derek 197608     0 Apr 29 10:03 agent_workspace\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Derek 197608 19290 Apr 29 10:03 cli.py\n=== tests count ===\n46\n=== inner tests? ===\n__pycache__\ntest_auto_routing_integration.py\ntest_complexity_heuristic.py\ntest_consciousness_api.py\ntest_consensus_audit_jsonl.py\ntest_consensus_cli.py\ntest_consensus_coordinator.py\ntest_consensus_runtime.py\ntest_consensus_websocket.py\ntest_domain_selector.py\ntest_goal_cli.py\ntest_goal_consensus.py\ntest_goal_pipeline.py\ntest_goal_proposer.py\ntest_goal_store.py\ntest_goal_translator.py\ntest_workflow_persistence.py\n=== agent_workspace root ===\nagents\nerror.txt\n=== agent_workspace inner ===\nagents\nerror.txt\n"}],"details":{"cwd":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584359132}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"63030483","parentId":"0d90e0e8","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:14:20.478Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — the M006-PLAN.md seems to have diverged from reality. Let me check:\n\n1. M006-CONTEXT.md talked about:\n   - Moving `src/` into `backend/`\n   - Consolidating root `tests/` (~50 files) + inner `tests/` (~16) into `backend/tests/`\n   - Deleting inner docs/agent_workspace copies\n   \n2. But M006-PLAN.md (final plan) focuses on:\n   - `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/` as a single directory rename\n   - `tests/` stays at root (UNMOVED)\n   - `src/` stays at root (UNMOVED)\n   - `migrations/` stays at root\n\n3. M007-ROADMAP.md says:\n   - S01: Rename heretek-swarm/ to backend/ via git mv\n   - S02: Rewrite imports and CI paths\n   - S03: Verify clean clone and full integration\n\nSo the PLAN.md was significantly refined from what CONTEXT.md originally described. The scope was narrowed. The M006-PLAN.md is the authoritative reference for M007 execution.\n\nBut wait — there are still open questions from M006-CONTEXT.md that haven't been resolved:\n- Inner `tests/` directory: 16 files, still exists at `heretek-swarm/tests/`. M006-PLAN says tests stay at root. So inner tests presumably moved out? No, the plan says `tests/` stays at root but says nothing about the inner `tests/`. Hmm.\n- Inner `agent_workspace/`: exists at both root and inner levels\n- `src/` directory: stays at root, but has stale `bandit -r src/` references that CI will need to fix\n\nWait, let me re-read M006-PLAN. It says tests/ stays at root (UNMOVED) and that the inner heretek-swarm/ directory will be moved wholesale. So the inner tests/ would move to backend/tests/. But then the plan's import survey says all test imports use `heretek_swarm.*` package paths — they're package-relative, not filesystem-path-relative. So if inner tests stay at `backend/tests/` (moved from `heretek-swarm/tests/`), their imports will still work.\n\nActually, the M006-PLAN.md says tests/ is UNMOVED (root tests), and then there's also an inner tests/ at heretek-swarm/tests/. When `git mv heretek-swarm backend` happens, the inner tests go to `backend/tests/`. The root `tests/` stays. So after migration, we'd have tests at both `tests/` and `backend/tests/`.\n\nWait, but the M007 ROADMAP says \"heretek-swarm/ renamed to backend/\". That would move everything including inner tests/ and inner agent_workspace/. The boundary map shows:\n```\nheretek-swarm/                        ← repo root (unchanged)\n├── backend/                          ← heretek-swarm/ renamed\n│   └── heretek_swarm/              ← Python package (unchanged)\n├── swarm-dashboard/\n├── docs/\n├── agent_workspace/\n└── .github/workflows/\n```\n\nSo the ROADMAP doesn't show `backend/tests/` — only `backend/heretek_swarm/`. But git mv would move the entire directory including inner tests/ and inner agent_workspace/.\n\nOK, the key gray areas I see:\n\n1. **Inner `tests/` at `heretek-swarm/tests/`**: 16 test files. M006-PLAN says these move with the directory (no Python changes needed). But do these tests currently pass? Have they been maintained? Are they duplicates of root tests?\n\n2. **Inner `agent_workspace/`**: Both root and inner copies. Will the inner copy (now at `backend/agent_workspace/`) conflict with root `agent_workspace/`? Are there path references between them?\n\n3. **`src/` directory**: Staying at root. But M006 said two CLI entry points existed — has that been resolved? `src/cli.py` (19KB) vs `heretek_swarm/cli.py` (likely larger). Are both functional?\n\n4. **CI `bandit -r src/` references**: M006-PLAN says to change these. But the plan says to change `bandit -r src/` → `bandit -r backend/`. This assumes `src/` is obsolete or empty. What about `src/cli.py` itself?\n\n5. **Garbage files**: M006 mentioned root garbage files `=X.Y.Z` — still there?\n\n6. **The open questions from M006-CONTEXT.md**: Were they all resolved during M006 audit? Let me check if there's a closure note.\n\nLet me now check the current CI files and a few more things before asking questions.\n\nActually, let me be strategic. I need to identify the 3-5 behavioral or architectural unknowns that materially change what gets built in M007. Let me focus on:\n- What's ambiguous in the execution plan\n- What risks haven't been addressed\n- What decisions from M006 might have been incorrect\n\nLet me check a few more things quickly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xsa227lf","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== Garbage files ===\" && ls -la =* 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \"=== inner tests pass? ===\" && python -c \"import ast, os; d='heretek-swarm/tests'; [print(f'{f}: {len([n for n in ast.walk(ast.parse(open(os.path.join(d,f)).read())) if isinstance(n, (ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom))])} imports') for f in os.listdir(d) if f.endswith('.py')]\" 2>/dev/null | head -20 && echo \"=== CI file references ===\" && grep -rn \"heretek-swarm\" .github/workflows/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== docker-compose refs ===\" && grep -n \"heretek-swarm\" docker-compose.yml 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== pyproject refs ===\" && grep -n \"heretek-swarm\" pyproject.toml 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":162811,"output":1392,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":164203,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778584359132}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"8210369d","parentId":"ca19f23d","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:14:46.939Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me also check the `src/` directory and the pre-commit config:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_t7qphgn5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== Pre-commit refs ===\" && grep -n \"heretek-swarm\\|src/\" .pre-commit-config.yaml 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== src/cli.py imports ===\" && head -30 src/cli.py && echo \"=== .dockerignore refs ===\" && grep -n \"heretek-swarm\" .dockerignore 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== Dockerfile refs ===\" && grep -n \"heretek-swarm\" heretek-swarm/Dockerfile"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":164771,"output":175,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":164946,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778584460817}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"d1fce9b8","parentId":"bcfb2806","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:15:20.444Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No pre-commit config references found. Let me also check what the inner tests directory looks like and whether it's separate from the root tests.\n\nNow let me think about what are the REAL gray areas for M007:\n\n1. **Scope of rename vs. M006-PLAN divergence**: M006-CONTEXT.md described a broader scope (consolidate src/, merge tests, etc.) but M006-PLAN.md narrowed to `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/` only. The M007 ROADMAP follows the narrow scope. Is this the right scope? Should we do more cleanup now?\n\n2. **Inner `tests/`** at `heretek-swarm/tests/` (16 files): These will move to `backend/tests/`. Are these tests maintained? Do they pass? They import from `heretek_swarm.*` (package path, unchanged). But the test runner needs to know about them.\n\n3. **Inner `agent_workspace/`**: Both root and inner copies exist. After rename, the inner one becomes `backend/agent_workspace/`. Is this intentional? Are both needed?\n\n4. **`src/` directory**: Staying at root. CI currently has `bandit -r src/` — should this change to `bandit -r backend/`? Is `src/cli.py` still needed?\n\n5. **pyproject.toml name**: The package NAME is `heretek-swarm` (with dash), but the Python package is `heretek_swarm` (with underscore). The rename of the directory doesn't change the package name. But should it? The M006-PLAN says no Python code changes, but the pyproject.toml `name` field stays `heretek-swarm`.\n\n6. **Docker/Compose build**: After rename, `docker compose build` needs `backend/Dockerfile`, and the Dockerfile needs its COPY paths updated.\n\n7. **The garbage files**: M006 mentioned `=X.Y.Z` files in root directory. These should be cleaned up.\n\n8. **`db` files in heretek-swarm/**: `heretek_swarm.db` and `test_ws_integration.db` are in the heretek-swarm/ directory. Are these build artifacts? Should they move or be gitignored?\n\n9. **`src/agent_workspace/`**: There's also an `agent_workspace` under `src/`. Another duplicate.\n\nLet me focus my questions on the 2-3 most materially important unknowns. The biggest ones are:\n\n1. **What exactly needs to happen to tests/**: The M006-PLAN says root `tests/` stays, inner `tests/` moves with the directory to `backend/tests/`. After M007, where should pytest look for tests? Both locations?\n\n2. **What about src/**: Is `src/cli.py` maintained or dead? Should we clean it up in M007 or defer?\n\n3. **The agent_workspace duplication**: Both root and inner (and src/) copies exist.\n\nLet me now formulate my first structured question round. This is \"complex\" mode (from PROJECT.md shape), so I need 3-4 researched options per question.\n\nActually, I already have a lot of information. Let me check one more thing about the inner tests to see if they're actually test files that run or stale copies.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_zppu8xhl","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== Inner tests content check ===\" && for f in heretek-swarm/tests/*.py; do echo \"--- $f ---\"; head -5 \"$f\"; done && echo \"=== src/agent_workspace ===\" && ls src/agent_workspace/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== db files ===\" && ls -la heretek-swarm/*.db 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":164971,"output":845,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":165816,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778584486981}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"09e83528","parentId":"d1fce9b8","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:15:20.771Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zppu8xhl","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== Inner tests content check ===\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_auto_routing_integration.py ---\n\"\"\"\nIntegration tests for auto-routing and multi-round consensus.\n\nTests the end-to-end flow:\n1. Complex prompt auto-routes through consensus\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_complexity_heuristic.py ---\n\"\"\"\nTests for ComplexityHeuristic — automatic consensus detection.\n\nCovers: keyword matching, length thresholding, combined scoring,\nthreshold configuration, edge cases, and determinism.\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_consciousness_api.py ---\n\"\"\"\nTests for Consciousness API — M010 S04 T02.\n\nVerifies the data pipeline from live agent state → EnhancedConsciousnessPlugin\n→ /api/consciousness/* endpoints is real (not stub data).\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_consensus_audit_jsonl.py ---\n\"\"\"\nTests for ConsensusAuditTrail JSONL fallback (--no-infra mode).\n\nVerifies that audit events are written to a JSONL file when\nstorage_backend=\"jsonl\", using a background writer thread with\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_consensus_cli.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for the `heretek-swarm consensus` CLI command.\"\"\"\n\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock, patch\n\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_consensus_coordinator.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for ConsensusCoordinator — bridge between agents and MAKER voting.\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport os\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_consensus_runtime.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for AutonomousSwarm.run_consensus() runtime integration.\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nfrom unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock, patch\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_consensus_websocket.py ---\n\"\"\"\nTests for WebSocket broadcasting of consensus events (M009/S03/T02).\n\nVerifies that the consensus API endpoints broadcast events through the\ndashboard WebSocket channel at the correct lifecycle points:\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_domain_selector.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for DomainSelector — topic-matching agent selection.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport time\n\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_goal_cli.py ---\n\"\"\"\nTests for the ``goal`` CLI command group (T04).\n\nVerifies that ``heretek-swarm goal list`` and ``heretek-swarm goal propose``\nare wired into the Click CLI and that the CLI runner can invoke them.\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_goal_consensus.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for GoalConsensus — goal-specific voting with 60% threshold.\n\nVerifies that:\n- _approval_ratio computes correctly (ignoring abstain)\n- _evaluate_threshold applies D024 ≥60% rule\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_goal_pipeline.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for the Goal Pipeline.\n\nVerifies that the autonomous goal cycle correctly:\n- Proposes a new goal when the queue is empty\n- Runs consensus voting on proposed goals\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_goal_proposer.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for GoalProposer — prompt generation and LLM response parsing.\n\nVerifies that:\n- generate_proposal_prompt() returns a non-empty, structured prompt\n- proposal_system_prompt() returns the Metis system prompt\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_goal_store.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for Goal persistence — FileGoalStore and Goal data model.\n\nVerifies that:\n- Goal.from_dict / to_dict round-trips correctly\n- Vote serialization is lossless\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_goal_translator.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for GoalToWorkflowTranslator.\n\nVerifies that:\n- Successful LLM response parses into nodes and edges\n- Bad JSON triggers the fallback mechanism\n--- heretek-swarm/tests/test_workflow_persistence.py ---\n\"\"\"Tests for workflow persistence — FileWorkflowStore and engine integration.\n\nVerifies that:\n- FileWorkflowStore CRUD operations work correctly\n- Atomic writes produce valid JSON even under simulated failure\n=== src/agent_workspace ===\nerror.txt\n=== db files ===\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Derek 197608 0 May  1 13:52 heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm.db\n-rw-r--r-- 1 Derek 197608 0 May  1 13:55 heretek-swarm/test_ws_integration.db\n"}],"details":{"cwd":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584520770}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"213edb55","parentId":"09e83528","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:15:53.473Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me also quickly check the .gitignore to see if these .db files and inner tests are tracked:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_r3uzb3bt","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== Are inner tests tracked? ===\" && git ls-files heretek-swarm/tests/ 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \"=== Are db files tracked? ===\" && git ls-files heretek-swarm/*.db 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== Are garbage files tracked? ===\" && git ls-files '=*' 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== Is src/agent_workspace tracked? ===\" && git ls-files src/agent_workspace/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== .gitignore db refs ===\" && grep \"db\" .gitignore 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":166774,"output":213,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":166987,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778584520771}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"b5846193","parentId":"213edb55","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:15:53.657Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_r3uzb3bt","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== Are inner tests tracked? ===\nheretek-swarm/tests/test_auto_routing_integration.py\nheretek-swarm/tests/test_complexity_heuristic.py\nheretek-swarm/tests/test_consciousness_api.py\nheretek-swarm/tests/test_consensus_audit_jsonl.py\nheretek-swarm/tests/test_consensus_cli.py\n=== Are db files tracked? ===\n=== Are garbage files tracked? ===\n=0.2.0\n=0.23.0\n=1.1.0\n=1.8.0\n=2.3.0\n=24.0.0\n=3.12.0\n=3.5.0\n=4.0.0\n=4.1.0\n=6.98.0\n=8.0.0\n=== Is src/agent_workspace tracked? ===\nsrc/agent_workspace/error.txt\n=== .gitignore db refs ===\n*.db\nThumbs.db\n"}],"details":{"cwd":"C:\\Users\\Derek\\Desktop\\heretek-swarm"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584553657}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"92a76946","parentId":"b5846193","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:17:19.725Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the complete picture. Let me summarize what I've found:\n\n**Current state (matches M006-PLAN.md expectations):**\n\n1. **`heretek-swarm/`** — the project subdirectory containing:\n   - `heretek_swarm/` — the Python package (430+ .py files)\n   - `tests/` — 16 tracked test files (consensus/goal/workflow tests)\n   - `agent_workspace/` — inner workspace copy\n   - `docs/` — inner docs copy (actors/ only?)\n   - `Dockerfile` — backend container\n   - `LICENSE`\n   - `.db` files (zero-byte, gitignored)\n\n2. **Root `tests/`** — 46 test files, tracked\n\n3. **`src/`** — CLI entry point + agent_workspace copy, tracked\n\n4. **Garbage `=X.Y.Z` files** — 12 tracked zero-byte files at root\n\n5. **CI/workflow files** — 4 files with `heretek-swarm/` path references\n   - ci.yml: 2 references\n   - ci-cd.yml: multiple references (based on M006 plan)\n   - docker-compose.yml: 1 reference (Dockerfile path)\n   - pyproject.toml: 9 references including `where`, `source`, `src`, plus URLs\n\n**Key gray areas / decisions needed for M007:**\n\n1. **Inner tests at `heretek-swarm/tests/`**: 16 tracked files. After `git mv`, they become `backend/tests/`. Root `tests/` stays at root. This means tests will be split across two locations. The M006-PLAN says this is fine. But:\n   - Do these tests currently pass? (they import from `heretek_swarm.*` — should be fine)\n   - Should they be consolidated into root `tests/` during M007?\n   - The M007 ROADMAP doesn't mention them at all\n\n2. **Inner `agent_workspace/` duplication**: Root (canonical, 9 agents), inner (partial, 6 agents), and `src/agent_workspace/`. After rename, we'd have `agent_workspace/` (root), `backend/agent_workspace/` (inner), `src/agent_workspace/`. That's three copies.\n\n3. **`src/` directory**: M006-CONTEXT.md proposed consolidating into `backend/` but M006-PLAN.md left it at root. Current CI references `bandit -r src/` → should become `bandit -r backend/`. Is `src/` maintained or dead?\n\n4. **Garbage `=X.Y.Z` files**: 12 tracked zero-byte files. Cleanup in M007?\n\n5. **pyproject.toml `name` field**: Stays as `heretek-swarm` — this is the PyPI package name. Does the directory rename change any thinking here?\n\n6. **Dockerfile COPY paths**: Need updating (documented in plan). Also docker-compose.yml.\n\n7. **`.pre-commit-config.yaml`**: No path references found — safe.\n\nLet me identify the 3 TOP gray areas to ask about. I think the most important are:\n\n1. **Test directory split**: After rename, tests at `tests/` (root) AND `backend/tests/` (inner). Consolidate or keep split?\n2. **`src/` and workspace duplication**: Clean up in M007 or defer?\n3. **M007 scope**: Execute only what's in ROADMAP (3 slices) or include cleanup items from M006 that weren't executed?\n\nLet me formulate my structured questions.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Good. I've now built a complete picture. The M006 audit produced a detailed plan, but several execution-level decisions weren't fully resolved. Let me ask about the most material ones."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_z2ijjcx0","name":"ask_user_questions","arguments":{"questions":[{"header":"Test layout","id":"m007_tests_split","options":[{"description":"Move inner tests to root tests/, single pytest entry point. More conventional, easier CI.","label":"Consolidate to root tests/ (Recommended)","preview":"```\nbackend/heretek_swarm/   ← Python package only\n├── tests/               ← all 62 test files consolidated here\n├── .github/workflows/   ← pytest tests/ -v\n└── pyproject.toml       ← single test path\n```"},{"description":"Keep root tests/ and backend/tests/ separate. Less churn, but two test locations to remember.","label":"Leave split as-is","preview":"```\nbackend/\n├── heretek_swarm/\n└── tests/               ← 16 consensus/goal tests\ntests/                   ← 46 general tests\n```"},{"description":"Move root tests into backend/. Everything Python lives under one directory.","label":"Consolidate into backend/tests/"}],"question":"After `git mv heretek-swarm backend`, tests will live in two places: root `tests/` (46 files) and `backend/tests/` (16 consensus/goal/workflow files). M006-PLAN.md says this is fine — both import from `heretek_swarm.*` package paths. Should M007 consolidate these into a single location, or leave the split?"},{"header":"src/ cleanup","id":"m007_src_cleanup","options":[{"description":"Remove the root src/ directory. heretek_swarm/cli.py is the canonical CLI entry point.","label":"Delete src/ entirely (Recommended)","preview":"```bash\n# src/cli.py (19KB) — separate entry point\n# vs heretek_swarm/cli.py (63KB) — canonical CLI\n# CI references: bandit -r src/  →  bandit -r backend/\n```"},{"description":"Don't touch src/. M006-PLAN.md kept it separate; don't add scope creep to M007.","label":"Leave src/ at root"},{"description":"Merge the CLI surface but keep src/ directory structure minimal.","label":"Move src/cli.py into backend/"}],"question":"M006-CONTEXT.md proposed consolidating `src/` (contains `cli.py` entry point + `agent_workspace/`) into `backend/`, but M006-PLAN.md left it at root. CI still has `bandit -r src/` references. Should M007 clean up `src/` or leave it alone?"},{"header":"Cleanup scope","id":"m007_cleanup_scope","options":[{"description":"Delete garbage files and duplicate workspaces. One-stop shop — leave the repo clean.","label":"Include cleanup in M007 (Recommended)","preview":"```bash\n# Cleanup items:\nrm =0.2.0 =0.23.0 ... =8.0.0  # 12 garbage files\ngit rm heretek-swarm/agent_workspace/  # inner duplicate\nrm heretek-swarm/*.db  # already gitignored\n```"},{"description":"Just the 3 ROADMAP slices. Defer cleanup to a separate milestone to keep M007 tight.","label":"Stick to rename + config only"},{"description":"Delete the =X.Y.Z files (low risk, obvious junk) but leave workspace duplication for later.","label":"Partial: garbage files only"}],"question":"There are 12 tracked garbage files at root (`=0.2.0`, `=8.0.0`, etc.), duplicated `agent_workspace/` at three levels (root, inner, src/), and zero-byte `.db` files. Should M007 include a cleanup pass for these, or stick strictly to the rename + config edits?"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":167219,"output":1761,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":168980,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778584553657}}
