ication"}],"question":"M006-PLAN.md documents Dockerfile COPY path updates and docker-compose.yml changes. Should M007 require a full `docker compose build` as part of verification, or is config-level validation (docker compose config parses, no stale path references) sufficient?"},{"header":"Execution order","id":"m007_execution_order","options":[{"description":"Consolidate tests + delete inner copies BEFORE git mv, then config edits, then cleanup. Cleanest result.","label":"Pre-mv consolidation (Recommended)","preview":"```\nPhase 1: Consolidate inner tests/ → root tests/\nPhase 2: Delete inner docs/, agent_workspace/, db files\nPhase 3: Edit pyproject.toml paths\nPhase 4: git mv heretek-swarm backend\nPhase 5: Dockerfile + docker-compose + CI edits\nPhase 6: Delete src/, garbage =X.Y.Z files\nPhase 7: Full verification\n```"},{"description":"Do git mv first (simplest), then consolidate tests and clean up after.","label":"Rename first, cleanup after"},{"description":"All file moves (tests, cleanup) in one commit, config edits in another, verification last.","label":"Two-commit approach"}],"question":"With the expanded scope (test consolidation, src deletion, inner cleanup), what execution order do you prefer?"}],"response":{"endInterview":false,"answers":{"m007_inner_cleanup":{"selected":"Delete both inner copies (Recommended)","notes":""},"m007_docker_verify":{"selected":"Full docker build required","notes":""},"m007_execution_order":{"selected":"Pre-mv consolidation (Recommended)","notes":""}}},"cancelled":false},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778584924630}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M007.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"fd904e35","parentId":"a20e9f63","timestamp":"2026-05-12T11:23:32.282Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All three answers picked \"Recommended\". Let me now do the depth verification. Let me summarize what I've understood:\n\n**M007 scope (expanded from M006-PLAN):**\n\n1. **Pre-mv consolidation** (Phase 1-2):\n   - Move inner `heretek-swarm/tests/` (16 files) → root `tests/`\n   - Delete inner `heretek-swarm/docs/` (only actors/README.md)\n   - Delete inner `heretek-swarm/agent_workspace/` (partial copy)\n   - Delete zero-byte `.db` files in heretek-swarm/\n\n2. **Config edits** (Phase 3):\n   - Edit `pyproject.toml`: `where`, `source`, `src` directives from `heretek-swarm` → `backend`\n\n3. **Directory rename** (Phase 4):\n   - `git mv heretek-swarm backend`\n\n4. **Post-mv config edits** (Phase 5):\n   - `backend/Dockerfile`: COPY paths (3 lines)\n   - `docker-compose.yml`: Dockerfile path (1 line)\n   - `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: ruff + pytest paths (2+ lines)\n   - `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml`: ruff + mypy + bandit + pytest paths\n   - `.github/workflows/load-test.yml`: check for path references\n\n5. **Cleanup** (Phase 6):\n   - Delete `src/` directory entirely\n   - `git rm` 12 garbage `=X.Y.Z` files\n\n6. **Verification** (Phase 7):\n   - `pip install -e .` works\n   - `python -c \"import heretek_swarm\"` works\n   - `ruff check backend/ tests/` passes\n   - `pytest tests/ -v --cov=backend` passes\n   - `docker compose config` parses\n   - `docker compose build` succeeds (full docker build required)\n   - `git grep \"heretek-swarm/\" -- ':!.gsd/'` returns empty (except historical/URL references)\n\nNow let me print the depth summary and do the depth check.\n\nActually, let me think about what still isn't covered:\n- What they're building: ✅ A restructured repo with `backend/heretek_swarm/` as the Python package dir\n- Why it needs to exis