.gsd.migrating/activity/002-discuss-milestone-M005.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"1f843ace","parentId":"623e06aa","timestamp":"2026-05-10T23:04:28.082Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — I now have a solid picture. The milestone is clear and well-planned. Let me ask about the gray areas before writing the context.\n\n**Milestone M005: Document architecture and compress flat actor API surface**\n\nWhat I see:\n- **S01 (Write docs)** is fully planned with clear tasks\n- **S02 (structlog consolidation)** has no concrete plan yet — core.py has inline `structlog.configure(...)` with 8 processors\n- **S03 (flat actor compression)** has no concrete plan — flat files like `alpha.py` (282 lines), `beta.py` (299), `charlie.py` (393), `steward.py` (840), `echo.py` (749) contain real implementations, not just re-exports\n\nA few things I want to clarify:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"ollama_tc_1","name":"ask_user_questions","arguments":{"questions":"[{\"id\": \"arch_depth\", \"header\": \"ARCHITECTURE.md\", \"question\": \"How deep should the ARCHITECTURE.md rewrite go?\", \"options\": [{\"label\": \"Update paths + add sections (Recommended)\", \"description\": \"Keep current 9-section TOC, fix all stale src/ paths to heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/, add Package Structure and Actor Base Class & Mixins sections\", \"preview\": \"## SECTIONS TO RETAIN\\n- System Overview\\n- Actor Architecture\\n- Memory System\\n- Event Mesh\\n- Configuration System\\n- Security\\n- Observability\\n- Monitoring Setup\\n- References\\n\\n## SECTIONS TO ADD\\n- Package Structure (actual directory tree)\\n- Actor Base Class & Mixins (AgentActor hierarchy + 10-mixin reference)\\n\\n## FIXES\\n- All src/heretek_swarm/ -> heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/\\n- Flat file refs (triad.py) -> subpackage refs (actors/triad/agent.py)\\n- Stale health scores removed or updated\"}, {\"label\": \"Full rewrite from scratch\", \"description\": \"Discard the old doc entirely, write a new one focused only on current codebase structure with no legacy references\"}, {\"label\": \"Minimal fixup only\", \"description\": \"Just replace src/heretek_swarm/ with heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/ and update file paths, keep everything else as-is\"}]}, {\"id\": \"flat_actor_approach\", \"header\": \"Flat Actors\", \"question\": \"For S03 (compress flat actors): what's the approach for files like alpha.py (282 lines), beta.py (299), steward.py (840) etc.?\", \"options\": [{\"label\": \"Thin re-exports to subpackages (Recommended)\", \"description\": \"Move implementation into existing subpackages (e.g. actors/triad/agent.py), leave a re-export stub. Files with no matching subpackage get extracted into new ones\"}, \"preview\": \"## Example: alpha.py -> thin re-exports\\n\\n```python\\n# heretek_swarm/actors/alpha.py\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nAlpha agent - thin re-export.\\n\\nImplementation moved to heretek_swarm.actors.triad.agent\\nfor consistency with the subpackage convention.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom heretek_swarm.actors.triad import AlphaAgent\\n\\n__all__ = [\\\"AlphaAgent\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n## Flat files to compress:\\n- **alpha.py** (282L) -> re-export from triad/\\n- **beta.py** (299L) -> re-export from triad/\\n- **charlie.py** (393L) -> re-export from triad/\\n- **steward.py** (840L) -> re-export from triad/\\n- **historians.py** (1353L) -> new subpackage?\\n- **metis.py** (1110L) -> new subpackage?\\n- **empath.py** (1085L) -> new subpackage?\\n- **perceiver.py** (911L) -> re-export from perceiver_plus/\\n- **echo.py** (749L) -> new subpackage?\\n- **coder.py** (979L) -> new subpackage?\\n- **explorer.py** (1317L) -> re-export from explorer/\\n- **catalyst.py** (1135L) -> new subpackage?\"}, {\"label\": \"Leave flat files as-is\", \"description\": \"S03 only covers the files that are ALREADY re-exports from M001. The big flat files with real implementation stay flat\"}]}, {\"label\": \"Other — let me discuss\", \"description\": \"I have a different approach in mind\"}]}, {\"id\": \"structlog_approach\", \"header\": \"Structlog Config\", \"question\": \"For S02 (structlog consolidation): what's the target state?\", \"options\": [{\"label\": \"Single configure_logging() in logging/config.py (Recommended)\", \"description\": \"Move the inline structlog.configure() out of base/core.py into logging/config.py. Base/core.py imports configure_logging() and calls it once on import. Tests can override via pytest fixture\", \"preview\": \"## Target state\\n\\n```python\\n# heretek_swarm/logging/config.py\\ndef configure_logging(\\n    level: str = \\\"INFO\\\",\\n    json_format: bool = True,\\n    service_name: str = \\\"heretek-swarm\\\",\\n) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Single entry point for all structlog configuration.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    processors = [...]\\n    structlog.configure(processors=processors, ...)\\n\\n# Call once at the right time\\n```\\n\\n```python\\n# heretek_swarm/actors/base/core.py (after S02)\\nfrom heretek_swarm.logging.config import configure_logging\\nconfigure_logging()\\nlogger = structlog.get_logger(\\\"AgentActor\\\")\\n```\"}, {\"label\": \"Just document existing setup\", \"description\": \"Leave the structlog.configure() inline in core.py, just document it. Make S02 purely documentation\"}]}]"}}],"api":"ollama-chat","provider":"ollama","model":"deepseek-v4-flash:cloud","usage":{"input":174263,"output":1648,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":175911,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778454226237,"inferenceMetrics":{"tokensPerSecond":0,"totalDurationMs":41753.653841,"evalDurationMs":0,"promptEvalDurationMs":0}}}
