.gsd.migrating/activity/003-discuss-milestone-M001.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"dbaa3279","parentId":"1c829e40","timestamp":"2026-05-07T12:07:37.438Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\nThe user chose:\n1. Fixed absolute path - Define a constant like ~/.heretek-swarm/ or project root always\n2. Delete it - Remove it — likely a duplicate/leftover from a test run\n\nSo they want:\n- A fixed absolute path (not CWD-dependent)\n- Delete the orphan `steward1.json`\n\nNow I need to ask about what specific path to use and whether the code should be refactored to use a centralized constant.\n","thinkingSignature":"think-tag"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nGood — fixed path and clean up the orphan. Let me ask about specifics:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ng9p8snp7cnb_1","name":"ask_user_questions","arguments":{"questions":[{"header":"State Path","id":"fixed_path_choice","options":[{"description":"Clean separation — user data never mixes with repo","label":"~/.heretek-swarm/actor_states (Recommended)"},{"description":"Always project root — state stays with the repo clone","label":"<repo-root>/.actor_states"},{"description":"Customizable via HERETEK_STATE_DIR env var, defaulting to one of the above","label":"Hybrid: env var override"}],"question":"Where should the fixed absolute path point to?"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"MiniMax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":527,"output":366,"cacheRead":181435,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":182328,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778155645177}}
